Overlay patch 0025: mip filtering in Fast3D Metal samplers — SYNC WAVE 2
(reference 0029). Companion to 0021 rev2's mip chains: without a sampler mip
filter the chains are never read. Linear-filtered textures get trilinear +
4x anisotropy; the N64 three-point/nearest path keeps nearest-mip so the
authentic look is preserved. Samplers are created before texture uploads, so
this applies unconditionally — sampling a single-level texture with a mip
filter is well-defined (level 0). Fork note: Starship's `filter` is already
MTL::SamplerMinMagFilter (same type the Ship of Harkinian port compares).

--- a/libultraship/src/graphic/Fast3D/backends/gfx_metal.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/graphic/Fast3D/backends/gfx_metal.cpp
@@ -376,6 +376,15 @@
                                           : MTL::SamplerMinMagFilterNearest;
     sampler_descriptor->setMinFilter(filter);
     sampler_descriptor->setMagFilter(filter);
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0025): read the 0021-rev2 mip chains — trilinear +
+    // modest anisotropy on the linear path; nearest-mip preserves the
+    // three-point/nearest N64 look. Single-level textures sample level 0.
+    if (filter == MTL::SamplerMinMagFilterLinear) {
+        sampler_descriptor->setMipFilter(MTL::SamplerMipFilterLinear);
+        sampler_descriptor->setMaxAnisotropy(4);
+    } else {
+        sampler_descriptor->setMipFilter(MTL::SamplerMipFilterNearest);
+    }
     sampler_descriptor->setSAddressMode(gfx_cm_to_metal(cms));
     sampler_descriptor->setTAddressMode(gfx_cm_to_metal(cmt));
     sampler_descriptor->setRAddressMode(MTL::SamplerAddressModeRepeat);
